{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Valley of Shaveh.</b> That is its name, as its Targum renders לְמֵישַׁר מְפַנָּא — cleared of trees and of every obstacle." "<b>The King's Valley.</b> בֵּית רֵיסָא דְמַלְכָּא — a בֵּית רֵיס, which is thirty kanim, that was designated for the king to play there. And its midrash: עֵמֶק — for there all the nations were gathered and crowned Abraham over them as 'a prince of Elohim and a ruler.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The phrase 'בֵּית רֵיס א׳' uses א׳ as an abbreviation marker for אוֹמֶרֶת, 'meaning'; the play-midrash on עֵמֶק plays on the root שוה, 'to make equal/unanimous.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:40.022645203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}